    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Pacific cod, Queen Charlotte Sound and Hecate Strait\"\nparams:\n  stock_id: \"pcod_5abcd\"\n---\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n:::\n\n\n::: {.disclaimer}\nExploratory personal project. Not an official assessment and not a seafood recommendation.\n:::\n\n::::: {.columns}\n\n:::: {.column width=\"36%\"}\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"stock-card\">\n<div class=\"card-head\" style=\"background:#8e44ad;\">\n<div class=\"card-species\">Pacific cod</div>\n<div class=\"card-title\">Pacific cod, Queen Charlotte Sound and Hecate Strait</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"badges\">\n<span class=\"badge\" style=\"background:#8e959c;\">Not in DFO 2024 survey</span>\n<span class=\"badge tier\">Data tier B</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"stat\">1.61× LRP</div>\n<div class=\"stat-label\">Biomass relative to the limit reference point, 2019</div>\n<img class=\"spark\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"Sparkline of biomass relative to the limit reference point for Pacific cod, Queen Charlotte Sound and Hecate Strait\"/>\n<dl>\n<dt>Evidence</dt>\n<dd>Biomass relative to MSY only</dd>\n<dt>Managed by</dt>\n<dd>Fisheries and Oceans Canada (DFO)</dd>\n<dt>Status method</dt>\n<dd>Not reported</dd>\n<dt>RAM assessment period</dt>\n<dd>1953-2019</dd>\n<dt>Biomass estimates</dt>\n<dd>1956 to 2019</dd>\n</dl>\n<div class=\"fun\">Fun fact: Also known as grey cod.</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n::::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"4%\"}\n::::\n\n:::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](pcod_5abcd_files/figure-html/trend-1.png){width=768}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n\n[Download the 2-page rapid assessment (PDF)](../reports/output/rapid_assessment_pcod_5abcd.pdf){.btn .btn-primary}\n::::\n\n:::::\n\n\n\n## Management context\n\n\nText in quotation marks is copied exactly as published in DFO's 2024 Sustainability Survey for Fisheries, including any typos.\n\n- **Limit reference point, as described by DFO:** Not reported\n- **Upper stock reference, as described by DFO:** Not reported\n- **Limit used for this project's indicator:** TBlim from RAM (limit reference point used in the assessment)\n- **Management plan, as reported by DFO:** Not reported\n- **Managed by:** Fisheries and Oceans Canada (DFO)\n\n## Data gaps and caveats\n\n\n- Not included in DFO's 2024 Sustainability Survey, so there is no official status zone here.\n- No fishing-pressure ratio relative to MSY, so no Kobe plot.\n- Limit reference point taken or derived from RAM Legacy; DFO's current value may differ.\n\n[← Back to all stock cards](../cards.qmd)\n\n",
